WEBVTT

00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:05.020
The district tournament has finally started!

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:08.790
Our first match is with West Sakuragawa Challengers!

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:10.720
We'll give it our all and definitely win!

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.460
Center half, Furuya...

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:15.060
...Kota.

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:17.230
...That's what I thought.

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:23.700
Kota-kun got left out of the forward 
position, so the Furuyas revolted.{are revolting.}

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.210
They kept playing very selfishly.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:33.010
The other team parked the bus and we couldn't score.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.710
We got scored on instead, 
which only added to our troubles.

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:42.590
The team will fall apart like this!

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:44.220
Think about it yourselves.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:46.590
If you can't, you won't improve.{You can't improve if you don't. }

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:50.030
And now the match moves to the second half.

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:30.000
You two better start passing properly.

00:02:57.490 --> 00:03:01.760
Who's the one on the pitch that can see everything most clearly?{Who's the person on the pitch who can see everyone the most clearly? }

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:06.200
Oh yeah. I can't just watch; I have to call out.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:09.070
Because I'm the captain!

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:05.120
Wow, it's become Dango Soccer again.

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:07.830
Hey, shouldn't you give them some orders?

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:09.330
I already did.

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:10.560
Really? What did you say?

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:14.100
"Think about it yourselves."

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:16.070
That's all?

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.700
Oh?

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:30.620
Hey, hey. Are you gonna lose before playing us?

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:43.760
This is no good. It's just like before.

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:49.800
I have to tell them something to turn this around.

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:51.300
Anything...

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:55.410
We kept on attacking their goal during the first half.

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:59.880
But it's obvious that we won't get any more goals like this.

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:06.150
Think about it ourselves, huh?

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:07.450
Yes.

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:10.460
What do you need to do right now? What can you do?

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:13.130
Think about it long and hard.

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:18.060
First we need to draw those guys away from their goal.

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:20.570
Then a hole will appear in that wall.

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:22.030
In order to do that...

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:24.040
Everyone! Fall back!

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:27.810
Use the space in the middle!

00:05:28.670 --> 00:05:29.980
Yeah.

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:32.180
Ryuuji, pass it back!

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:46.430
I see.

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:48.190
Like that, huh?

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:03.510
That's good. Not a bad idea.

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:05.580
Hey! Don't let them shoot at will!

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:06.250
Mark them!

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:13.550
Don't let them pass!

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:14.120
Mark them!

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:32.570
Ouzou-kun passed it to Erika-chan!?

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:34.040
Shoot it!

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:47.620
Crap.

00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:54.260
We need to score now.

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:03.640
Backup!

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:09.810
No! It's too early!

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:18.380
That was close!

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:27.290
Give us the call on when to attack.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:33.100
Okay. I got it.

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:38.040
Now?

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:40.040
Ouzou-kun! More!

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:44.040
Lure them out more!

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:50.580
More, huh?

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:51.850
Roger that!

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:00.160
O-Ouzou-kun?

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:01.460
What is he doing?

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:04.530
Heh, it's working.

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:06.260
That guy...{That fool.}

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:09.870
Eh? Why is he dribbling back to their own goal?

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:11.500
I wonder.

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:16.480
What do I see here? Ouzou?

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:18.980
He's very interesting.

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:21.680
Eh? What are they doing?

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:24.980
Are they making fun of us?

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:47.570
Oh! So close!

00:08:57.820 --> 00:08:59.550
Reika-chan! Move!

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:04.660
Reika...

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:07.330
Onii-chan?

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:14.600
Nice, Erika-chan!{Erika-chan, nice!}

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:17.340
Nice your face!

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:19.070
Ouzou-kun! The right!

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:25.180
Your play is terrible, but your vision is brilliant.

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:38.220
It's in!

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:39.620
Yes!

00:10:34.850 --> 00:10:36.620
9-1!

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:38.820
Momoyama Predators win!

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:40.120
Bow!

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:43.520
Thank you very much!

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:46.490
Thank you very much!

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:51.100
Thank you!

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:51.100
Thanks!

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:55.330
We won, right?

00:10:55.330 --> 00:10:56.740
Yeah, we did!

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:57.970
We won!

00:10:57.970 --> 00:10:59.140
Yes, we won!

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:01.610
Of course! It's only the first round!

00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:04.980
But I can't believe we're playing games already!

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:08.010
We actually played in a match and won!{I got to play and we won!}

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:10.820
Yeah!

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:13.790
Yes! Yes!

00:11:13.790 --> 00:11:15.650
Onii-chan won!

00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:17.020
Wow, Shou!

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:19.660
He revived the team and actually won!{The team really revived and won! }

00:11:20.330 --> 00:11:22.630
Wow, that was a great match.

00:11:22.630 --> 00:11:25.830
They didn't get caught up in the chaos.

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:29.030
Instead, they gained confidence from it and achieved victory.

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:30.370
It was amazing.

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:33.340
I look forward to the next match.

00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:02.970
Wow!

00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:05.000
That looks delicious!

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:06.940
Wow, you're right!

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:09.110
Having your family run a yakiniku restaurant is amazing!

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:14.210
Eat up, everyone!

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:17.220
Mom told me that this food will raise everyone's stamina.

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:18.850
Really?

00:12:18.850 --> 00:12:20.120
Can I have some?

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:21.390
Sure, sure!

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:26.090
Delicious!

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:27.260
Really?

00:12:29.230 --> 00:12:30.760
So good!

00:12:30.760 --> 00:12:31.960
It's true!

00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:33.130
It's delicious!

00:12:33.130 --> 00:12:34.430
Try some, Reika-chan.

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:36.940
Okay.

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:42.010
Hey! Leave some for me!

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:44.710
Onii-chan makes himself stand out no matter where he is.

00:12:44.710 --> 00:12:46.980
His voice is so loud, that's why.

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:50.920
But I'm really happy.

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:52.580
Now's not the time for that.

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:57.860
Just let me be. I actually won the first match I took part in!

00:12:57.860 --> 00:13:00.390
And as a part of the Momoyama Predators, too!

00:13:00.390 --> 00:13:02.030
Yeah, I know!

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:06.530
We never thought we would play for the Momoyama Predators again.

00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:07.570
Yeah.

00:13:07.570 --> 00:13:10.040
My feelings are all mixed up right now.

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:14.810
But you three said you had cram school and couldn't play soccer anymore.

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:17.510
W-Well, that's true.

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:20.010
Our parents told us to stop.

00:13:20.010 --> 00:13:22.480
But thank goodness I didn't.

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:24.580
Soccer is so much fun, after all.

00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:26.080
Indeed.{Yeah, yeah.}

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:28.620
You're happy too, right?

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:31.960
Well, winning is better than losing, of course.

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:33.830
Right, Reika-chan?

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:36.290
Y-Yeah.

00:13:40.570 --> 00:13:42.200
How about you guys?

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:43.900
We don't really feel anything.

00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:47.440
The first round was just a warm up.

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:50.440
But you had a tough time during the first half.

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:53.580
That's because the positions you chose created problems.

00:13:54.410 --> 00:13:56.010
There was no problem.

00:13:56.010 --> 00:14:00.690
When you finally got into the rhythm in the second half, it was a blowout, right?

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:03.460
I'm sure you realized this during the match.

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:05.890
No matter how skilled you are,

00:14:05.890 --> 00:14:10.730
selfish play will make you lose control of the match.

00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:14.400
Our opponents will just get stronger and stronger.

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:18.370
The most important thing is for all of you to think about what you can do.

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:20.870
What should you do? Each and every one of you need to think.

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:23.610
Then you move as a team.

00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:29.080
This team is still new.

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:34.620
I'll be testing out many formations and tactics.

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:37.060
Positions, too.

00:14:37.690 --> 00:14:39.320
For the second round this afternoon,

00:14:39.320 --> 00:14:41.230
I'll go with the same formation.

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:46.260
We'll play again in the afternoon in the second round, right?{The second game in the afternoon is when we'll play, right? }

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:47.600
Who are we playing?

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:51.900
Whoever wins the match between Tsubakimori SC and Ootani FC.

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:54.570
I think we'll play Tsubakimori, definitely.

00:14:54.570 --> 00:14:57.480
The team Suguro-kun is on, right?

00:14:57.480 --> 00:14:58.340
Yes.

00:14:58.340 --> 00:15:02.710
Suguro-kun said he'll beat us no 
matter what, so this is a fated match.

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:04.620
Suguro, huh?

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:07.950
The triplets ran circles around him during the mini game,

00:15:08.890 --> 00:15:11.860
but during a real match which uses the entire pitch,

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:14.330
he can use his abilities to the max.

00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:16.260
We can't underestimate him.

00:15:16.730 --> 00:15:18.960
We have some time left until the second match.

00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:21.070
Don't let your body rest too much.

00:15:21.070 --> 00:15:22.230
Okay!

00:15:22.670 --> 00:15:26.500
Coach! Can we go watch the match between Tsubakimori and Ootani?

00:15:27.470 --> 00:15:28.970
Oh, that's right.

00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:30.940
Let's all go together, then.

00:15:30.940 --> 00:15:33.340
We'll pass.

00:15:33.340 --> 00:15:36.650
We know how good Tsubakimori is, anyway.

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:40.550
Shooting practice is more practical.

00:15:40.550 --> 00:15:42.790
They really go by their own pace.

00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:56.130
Oh, they're about to start.

00:15:56.130 --> 00:15:57.900
Eh? Where's Reika-chan?

00:15:57.900 --> 00:16:00.870
Now that you mention it, where did she go?

00:16:00.870 --> 00:16:03.370
Did she get lost?

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:05.840
Yeah, right. She probably went to the bathroom.

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:11.350
I'm sorry.

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:16.790
Maybe she's feeling down somewhere because of what happened in the first match?

00:16:19.760 --> 00:16:22.960
I'll go take a look.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:24.700
Come back soon, okay?

00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:29.670
Reika-chan!

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:32.770
She's not here. Where did she go?

00:16:32.770 --> 00:16:35.440
Did she go home?

00:16:35.440 --> 00:16:36.640
I hope not.

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:40.350
Reika-chan!

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:42.080
Shou-kun.

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:44.520
Why are you screaming?

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:47.720
Oh, have you seen Reika-chan?

00:16:47.720 --> 00:16:49.350
Did something happen to Saionji?

00:16:49.350 --> 00:16:52.190
Well, I couldn't find her.

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:54.030
Huh? Where's Kota-kun?

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:56.730
He went off to practice on his own.

00:16:56.730 --> 00:17:01.100
Looks like he's still pissed off on not being picked as a forward.

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:03.030
I see.

00:17:03.030 --> 00:17:05.770
I'll go look around some more.

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:09.270
Kota-kun's gone, too.

00:17:09.270 --> 00:17:10.280
Don't tell me...

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:13.910
Diet!? Are you making fun of soccer!?{Are you looking down on us!?}

00:17:23.860 --> 00:17:27.530
No way... No way...!

00:17:27.590 --> 00:17:30.530
You made so many mistakes during the match!

00:17:30.530 --> 00:17:33.300
Stop fooling around!

00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:39.640
Oh no!

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:41.740
I-I must stop them, as the captain!

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:48.950
Erika-chan!

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:52.050
Can I borrow Zach for a bit?

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:53.790
Eh? Why?

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:57.320
Zach, I need your help. Can you come with me?

00:17:57.320 --> 00:18:01.160
No way. Zach only listens to me.

00:18:02.360 --> 00:18:03.930
Thank you!

00:18:04.460 --> 00:18:06.400
I'll be borrowing him!

00:18:06.400 --> 00:18:09.400
No way! When did Zach get so close to him?

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:13.810
I'm looking for Reika-chan. You know who she is, right?

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:41.070
H-Hello.

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:46.440
You better keep on winning, for our sake.

00:18:46.440 --> 00:18:47.370
Okay.

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:48.970
Thank you. We'll do our best.

00:18:48.970 --> 00:18:50.110
Later.

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:55.750
Oh yeah. One of the triplets is #9 on the Predators, right?

00:18:56.350 --> 00:18:57.120
Yeah.

00:18:57.120 --> 00:19:00.850
I saw him take that huge girl with him over there.

00:19:00.850 --> 00:19:02.190
Eh?

00:19:02.190 --> 00:19:05.290
He looked really scary, so that caught my eye.{I noticed.}

00:19:06.360 --> 00:19:07.830
Thank you!

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:08.990
Zach!

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:34.320
Wait up!

00:19:37.520 --> 00:19:38.590
S-Shou-kun?

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:41.060
What are you doing!?

00:19:41.060 --> 00:19:44.230
Don't fight, Kota-kun! We're teammates!

00:19:44.230 --> 00:19:45.830
Reika-chan's a girl, too!

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:48.070
We have a match soon, too!

00:19:48.070 --> 00:19:50.030
N-No.

00:19:50.030 --> 00:19:52.940
I asked Kota-kun.

00:19:53.810 --> 00:19:58.680
I want to practice on how to defend properly so I won't be scared during the match.

00:19:58.740 --> 00:20:03.680
I'll just keep on being a burden if I don't do so.

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:07.190
I don't want that. I want to do what I can.

00:20:07.650 --> 00:20:09.350
Reika-chan.

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:12.490
I see.

00:20:12.490 --> 00:20:13.790
Thank goodness.

00:20:13.790 --> 00:20:16.130
What were you imagining!?

00:20:16.230 --> 00:20:18.400
Stop fooling around!

00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:21.400
N-No, it's nothing. Sorry.

00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:25.900
Seems like you were pissed off about the positions, so I...

00:20:25.900 --> 00:20:28.110
I decide when to kick the ball.

00:20:28.110 --> 00:20:30.910
Why would I just storm off like that?

00:20:30.910 --> 00:20:34.410
I'll prove during the match that I'm most suited to be a forward.

00:20:34.880 --> 00:20:36.150
I see.

00:20:36.150 --> 00:20:40.890
Kota-kun and Reika-chan are both thinking about what's best for the team.

00:20:40.890 --> 00:20:43.760
I keep on being mistaken.

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:46.120
I fail as the captain.

00:20:46.120 --> 00:20:47.260
Okay!

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:48.790
I'll practice with you!

00:20:48.790 --> 00:20:51.360
It's easier with more people on defense, right?

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:54.400
Do whatever you want.

00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:55.870
Okay.

00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:02.810
Reika-chan, don't stop! Move!

00:21:05.640 --> 00:21:07.910
Hey! Don't give up so easily!

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:09.350
Okay!

00:21:09.350 --> 00:21:12.120
Stall them, even if it's for one second!

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:14.990
Destroy the attacking player's rhythm!

00:21:14.990 --> 00:21:17.920
Even if you aren't skilled, your 
tenacity is very hard to shake off.

00:21:18.760 --> 00:21:19.860
Okay!

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:27.700
Yes, Reika-chan! Like that!

00:21:27.700 --> 00:21:29.470
Not enough!

00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:34.340
Oh no. One more time!

00:22:02.370 --> 00:22:04.000
Where did you go?

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:05.070
Had to take care of something.

00:22:05.640 --> 00:22:07.170
How's the match?

00:22:07.170 --> 00:22:08.540
It's a one-sided game.

00:22:20.550 --> 00:22:22.090
That's a hat trick.

00:22:22.090 --> 00:22:24.560
Eh? Suguro-kun?

00:22:29.030 --> 00:22:33.230
Was Tsubakimori SC this strong?

00:22:33.230 --> 00:22:35.230
They had the skill.

00:22:35.230 --> 00:22:40.240
Ever since Suguro-kun became the core of their team, they got their attacking pattern down pat.

00:22:40.240 --> 00:22:43.410
Looks like it'll be much harder than the first match.

00:22:55.250 --> 00:22:58.490
"You're next," huh?

00:22:58.490 --> 00:23:00.220
What a simple guy.

00:23:00.220 --> 00:23:03.830
Well, let's show him the difference in skill.

00:24:35.150 --> 00:24:38.560
Okay! Next up is our match with Tsubakimori SC!

00:24:38.560 --> 00:24:41.590
The fated match between Suguro-kun and the triplets!

00:24:41.590 --> 00:24:44.130
The managers' fated match, too!

00:24:44.130 --> 00:24:45.760
That's really embarrassing.

00:24:45.760 --> 00:24:48.100
But Suguro-kun's really pumped up!

00:24:48.100 --> 00:24:51.440
Um, can we do anything to stop him?

00:24:51.440 --> 00:24:54.710
Next episode of Ginga e Kickoff!! Suguro Special!
